		(instances (project "CostasLink-PYNQ-Z2" (path "/24723b42-5fe3-4667-eb46-0acbb937e3f8/b9479df7-906a-9090-5596-bc60e4422e88" (reference "#PWR") (unit 1)))))
	(text_box "Fit this block to work with ONE antenna per board: connect the antenna to ANT and run two short SMA leads, TX ANT -> SW\nTX and SW RX -> RX ANT (1 ns each), and let the FPGA drive TR_A / TR_B (B = not A): A HIGH, B low = receive (ANT to RF2\n= SW RX); A low, B high = transmit (ANT to RF1 = SW TX).  Without this block, two antennas per board and two frequencies\n600 MHz apart: both carriers always on, no holds, no turnaround.  How a pair keeps its frequency with one antenna each:\nthe VERIFIER transmits on its TCXO (JP201 on TCXO) and the PROVER's Costas loop locks its VCXO to that carrier; the\nprover's TX synthesizer runs from that VCXO (REF OUT -> REF IN, JP201 on REF IN: a transponder), so its reply is at the\nverifier's own frequency and phase.  While either board transmits its loop HOLDs (LOOP_HOLD, a sample-and-hold on the\nintegrator: 0.1 rad after 6 ms typical), and when it listens again the carrier it hears is the one it was locked to, so\nthe loop resumes instead of re-acquiring (3.8 ms from 30 kHz off).  ONE board carries the lead: both with it would be a\nring of two VCXOs with no reference, wandering together to a rail.  sim/budget.py section 2b and PLAN.md section 14 have\nthe numbers." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.3200 24.1300 0) (size 109.2200 21.5900)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "12cfa278-15f6-d55c-dbbd-6676fd2a241c"))
	(text_box "ANT, the antenna: 5.8 GHz\n(4.9-5.9 in spec) | out:\n+9.1 dBm (TX less 0.7 dB)\n| in: whatever arrives,\nless 0.7 dB | ABS MAX +27\ndBm at the switch (the LNA\nbehind SW RX: +1)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 87.6300 73.6600 0) (size 26.6700 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "76c8b2f9-4954-9d3b-9377-8682359ad2ce"))
	(text_box "SW TX: from TX ANT (+9.8 dBm)\nor a PA (<= +25 dBm without a\nlimiter) | 27 dB (min) to SW\nRX: -17.2 dBm leaks into the\nreceiver while transmitting; a\nPA over +25 dBm wants a\nlimiter ahead of the LNA (+1\ndBm abs max)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 231.1400 69.8500 0) (size 30.4800 16.5100)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "342bf0f4-21cb-3123-b07d-d2bf39755c49"))
	(text_box "SW RX: to RX ANT or the LNA |\nthe rest state (A high, B low)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 231.1400 123.1900 0) (size 29.2100 6.3500)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8da07629-2b9a-c20d-6cd8-01f3184561bd"))
	(text_box "J303: TR_A, TR_B and ground\nfor an external switch module\n(B made here by U402)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 41.9100 175.2600 0) (size 27.9400 7.6200)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "df286eee-9d2c-aa5b-5b24-f491b5d7bfd5"))
	(text_box "TR_A / TR_B: 0 / 3.3 V from the FPGA |\n30 ns edge-to-RF, 15 ns rise" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 80.0100 140.9700 0) (size 38.1000 6.3500)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b81893c6-3ed0-1062-ab2f-55f1cb493d3c"))
	(text_box "TR_A / TR_B: 0 / 3.3 V; A from the FPGA (header 27, also\nJ303), B = not A from U402 (since Response 14).  Truth table\n(datasheet): A low, B high: ANT-RF1 = SW TX (transmit).  A\nhigh, B low: ANT-RF2 = SW RX (receive): A's pull-ups (10 k\nhere, 2k2 on the PYNQ) hold A high until the gateware drives\nit, so B rests low and the switch rests in receive on both\nhosts.  30 ns from the edge to the RF settled; 15 ns rise;\nU402 adds about 3 ns to B." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 77.4700 170.1800 0) (size 55.8800 16.5100)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "271ca72f-d229-e2e1-7b82-7a5d9000bb92"))
	(text_box "HMC536MS8G, T/R switch (SPDT, GaAs,\nDC-6 GHz): 0.7 dB loss, 27 dB\nisolation at 5-6 GHz, +29 dBm for\n0.1 dB compression, 12 dB return\nloss at 4-6 GHz.  Switching: 30 ns\nfrom the control's 50 %% to the RF\nat 10 / 90 %% (tON, tOFF), 15 ns RF\nrise and fall (10-90 %%); the far\nend hears our reply 30 ns + the air\nafter TR_A falls.  Control 0 V (25\nuA) / 3-5 V, absolute maximum -0.5\nto +7.5 V; no supply pin (the\ncontrols power it).  DC blocks on\nall three RF pins (its datasheet).\nExposed pad to ground." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 132.0800 137.1600 0) (size 35.5600 27.9400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5921213a-8b91-7331-6145-069d266be919"))
	(text_box "TR A: the switch's A\ncontrol as the FPGA\ndrives it (0 / 3.3 V;\nhigh = receive) through\n453 ohm, /10 into 50 ohm\n(0 / 0.33 V): the 30 ns\nswitch timing." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 154.9400 120.6500 0) (size 25.4000 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a73d9234-3ad0-3b7a-6e56-8424d9e110f0"))
